                                                                        Y. Even if they do have the
                                                                        opening, from their point of
                                                                        view, if they let you
                                                                        transfer, they will
                                                                        definitely need to hire a
                                                                        replacement X, and you might
                                                                        turn out to suck at Y. So a
                                                                        rational manager will feel a
                                                                        strong pressure to leave
                                                                        well enough alone and let
                                                                        you keep doing X.

                                                                        There are a variety of ways
                                                                        for an employee to escape
                                                                        this situation, but the
                                                                        simplest one is just to find
                                                                        another company with an
